From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:02:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 90/92] web-app: Video.js player for chat videos and the
 fullscreen viewer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the native <video controls> in message bubbles and in
FullscreenMedia with Video.js 10's packaged skin (@videojs/react).
That brings controls that auto-hide 2 s after the pointer stops or
leaves while playing (the native ones covered the bottom of the
frame), YouTube-style hotkeys while the player has focus (space/k,
j/l and arrows seek, up/down volume, m, f, i for PiP, 0-9, < >),
touch tap-to-show-controls, double-tap seek and an error dialog for
formats the browser can't decode.

- Bubbles are sized from the sent dimensions like images (no jump
  when metadata loads), 350px fallback; preload=metadata.
- One medium at a time: a chat video starting pauses the voice
  singleton (now exported) and other chat videos; a voice message
  starting pauses videos. Scoped to video[data-chat-video].
- Volume/mute are remembered in localStorage.
- Keys inside a player stay with it: arrows don't move message-list
  focus (Message.tsx carve-out) or switch media in the viewer, and the
  type-to-focus-composer shortcut skips keys something already handled
  (keybindings.ts: !defaultPrevented), which had eaten m/k/0-9 while
  other letters still start a reply.
- The viewer's own buttons (save, close, prev/next) fade with the
  player's auto-hiding controls; hovered or focused ones stay visible.
- Labels follow the app language without Video.js's I18nProvider,
  which would inline all ~50 locale packs (+230 kB, the bundle has no
  code splitting). We provide its I18nContext ourselves: the active
  language's 3 kB pack is imported at runtime from videojs-locales/
  (the web-app serves them, URL relative to the document so subpath
  deployments work), our own locale strings fill in where no pack
  exists, English otherwise. App `pt` maps to pt-PT; Serbian keeps our
  Cyrillic strings (Video.js's sr pack is Latin script).

- Video-only bubbles: the player reaches the bubble's bottom edge (no
  black strip); time/✓ sit on the video above the control bar and fade
  with the controls while playing (CSS on the container's documented
  data-controls-visible state); reactions and a send error stay visible.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
